    "q-134509": {
      "dom_id": "step-q134509",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "$t\\sqrt[3]{2{t}^{2}}+\\sqrt[3]{2{t}^{5}}+\\sqrt[3]{54{t}^{2}}=$",
      "worked_solution": "We simplify each of the radical terms using the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t\\sqrt[3]{2{t}^{2}}+\\sqrt[3]{2{t}^{5}}+\\sqrt[3]{54{t}^{2}} & = \\\\ t\\sqrt[3]{2{t}^{2}}+\\sqrt[3]{{t}^{3}\\cdot 2{t}^{2}}+\\sqrt[3]{27\\cdot 2{t}^{2}} & = \\\\ t\\sqrt[3]{2{t}^{2}}+\\sqrt[3]{{t}^{3}\\cdot 2{t}^{2}}+\\sqrt[3]{{3}^{3}\\cdot 2{t}^{2}} & = \\\\ t\\sqrt[3]{2{t}^{2}}+\\sqrt[3]{{t}^{3}}\\cdot \\sqrt[3]{2{t}^{2}}+\\sqrt[3]{{3}^{3}}\\cdot \\sqrt[3]{2{t}^{2}} & = \\\\ t\\sqrt[3]{2{t}^{2}}+t\\sqrt[3]{2{t}^{2}}+3\\sqrt[3]{2{t}^{2}} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we combine the like terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t\\sqrt[3]{2{t}^{2}}+t\\sqrt[3]{2{t}^{2}}+3\\sqrt[3]{2{t}^{2}} & = \\\\ (t+t+3)\\sqrt[3]{2{t}^{2}} & = \\\\ (2t+3)\\sqrt[3]{2{t}^{2}} & \\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
